  "problem": {
    "id": "train-2767",
    "question": "It takes Polly 20 minutes to cook breakfast every day. She spends 5 minutes cooking lunch. She spends 10 minutes cooking dinner 4 days this week. The rest of the days she spends 30 minutes cooking dinner. How many minutes does Polly spend cooking this week?",
    "gold": "305",
    "answer": "Polly spends 20*7 =<<20*7=140>>140 minutes cooking breakfast.\nShe spends 5*7= <<5*7=35>>35 minutes cooking lunch.\nShe spends (10*4)+(30*3)= <<10*4+30*3=130>>130 minutes cooking dinner.\nTherefore, she spends 140+35+130=<<140+35+130=305>>305 minutes cooking this week.\n#### 305"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many minutes Polly spends cooking this week, we need to break down her cooking time for breakfast, lunch, and dinner separately and then sum them up.\n\n1. **Breakfast Cooking Time:**\n   Polly spends 20 minutes cooking breakfast every day. Since there are 7 days in a week, the total time spent on breakfast in a week is:\n   \\[\n   20 \\text{ minutes/day} \\times 7 \\text{ days} = 140 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Lunch Cooking Time:**\n   Polly spends 5 minutes cooking lunch every day. Therefore, the total time spent on lunch in a week is:\n   \\[\n   5 \\text{ minutes/day} \\times 7 \\text{ days} = 35 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Dinner Cooking Time:**\n   Polly spends 10 minutes cooking dinner 4 days this week. Therefore, the total time spent on dinner for these 4 days is:\n   \\[\n   10 \\text{ minutes/day} \\times 4 \\text{ days} = 40 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n   For the remaining 3 days of the week, she spends 30 minutes cooking dinner each day. Therefore, the total time spent on dinner for these 3 days is:\n   \\[\n   30 \\text{ minutes/day} \\times 3 \\text{ days} = 90 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n   Adding these two amounts together gives the total time spent on dinner for the week:\n   \\[\n   40 \\text{ minutes} + 90 \\text{ minutes} = 130 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total Cooking Time for the Week:**\n   Adding the time spent on breakfast, lunch, and dinner gives the total cooking time for the week:\n   \\[\n   140 \\text{ minutes} + 35 \\text{ minutes} + 130 \\text{ minutes} = 305 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of minutes Polly spends cooking this week is \\(\\boxed{305}\\).",
